IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition: ss 173A, 173B, 173C and 173H -- the duty of a company to tell the Registrar about its directors, chief executive officers, secretaries and auditors;
-- their duty to tell the company; the consents the company keeps; and the penalties.
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively). Part sgb2. Every top-level name begins with the label of its provision.
--
-- HOW IT READS. A company must tell the Registrar, by notice, within 14 days: of a new director, chief executive officer, secretary or auditor and the information the register needs (s 173A(1)(a)); of any change in an
-- appointment (b); of any change in the registered information (c); and of a director's ceasing to be qualified (d). The people themselves must give the company what it needs, as soon as practicable but within 14 days
-- (s 173B). The company must keep each director's signed consent, statement of non-disqualification and evidence of a change of name, and each secretary's signed consent, at its registered office (s 173C). Default is an
-- offence (s 173H). The sections cited for qualification (ss 148, 149, 149A, 154, 155, 155A, 155C, 155D) are later or earlier waves: whether a person has ceased to be qualified is a fact here.

§ `Section 173A: the company's notices to the Registrar, within 14 days`

DECLARE `s 173A act` IS ONE OF
    `s 173A(1)(a) furnish the Registrar by notice with the information required under section 173(3), (5), (6) or (7) for the person who has become a director, chief executive officer, secretary or auditor`
    `s 173A(1)(b) furnish the Registrar by notice with the particulars of the change in the information resulting from the change in the appointment`
    `s 173A(1)(c) furnish the Registrar by notice with the particulars of the change in the information`
    `s 173A(1)(d) furnish the Registrar by notice with the information about the person's ceasing to be qualified to act as a director`

-- (a): "within 14 days after a person becomes a director, chief executive officer, secretary or auditor, the information required under section 173(3), (5), (6) or (7), as the case may be".
-- src:14929 | 173A.—(1) A company must by notice furnish to the Registrar —
-- src:14931 | (a) within 14 days after a person becomes a director, chief
-- src:14932 | executive officer, secretary or auditor, the information
-- src:14933 | required under section 173(3), (5), (6) or (7), as the case
-- src:14934 | may be;
@ref s 173A(1)(a) (src:14929-14934)
GIVEN `the day the person became a director, chief executive officer, secretary or auditor` IS A DATE
      `the day the company furnished the notice` IS A DATE
      `the notice gives the information required under section 173(3), (5), (6) or (7), as the case may be` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 173A(1)(a) the company furnished the information in time` MEANS
    IF `the notice gives the information required under section 173(3), (5), (6) or (7), as the case may be` AND `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day the person became a director, chief executive officer, secretary or auditor` `the day the company furnished the notice` 14 Days
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company must by notice furnish to the Registrar (a) within 14 days after a person becomes a director, chief executive officer, secretary or auditor, the information required" (a period the text fixes in its own words: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a))

-- (b): "within 14 days after any change in the appointment of any director, chief executive officer, secretary or auditor, particulars of any change in the information ... resulting from the change in the appointment".
-- src:14938 | (b) within 14 days after any change in the appointment of any
-- src:14939 | director, chief executive officer, secretary or auditor,
-- src:14940 | particulars of any change in the information required to
-- src:14941 | be contained in the register of directors, chief executive
-- src:14946 | officers, secretaries or auditors mentioned in
-- src:14947 | section 173(3), (5), (6) or (7) resulting from the change
-- src:14948 | in the appointment;
@ref s 173A(1)(b) (src:14938-14948)
GIVEN `the day of the change in the appointment` IS A DATE
      `the day the company furnished the notice` IS A DATE
      `the notice gives the particulars of the change in the information resulting from the change in the appointment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 173A(1)(b) the company furnished the particulars of the change in time` MEANS
    IF `the notice gives the particulars of the change in the information resulting from the change in the appointment` AND `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day of the change in the appointment` `the day the company furnished the notice` 14 Days
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) within 14 days after any change in the appointment of any director, chief executive officer, secretary or auditor, particulars of any change in the information" (a period the text fixes in its own words: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a))

-- (c): "within 14 days after any change in the information required to be contained in the register ... mentioned in section 173(3), (5), (6) or (7), particulars of the change".
