@ref s 173A(1)(c) (src:14952-14955)
GIVEN `the day of the change in the information` IS A DATE
      `the day the company furnished the notice` IS A DATE
      `the notice gives the particulars of the change` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 173A(1)(c) the company furnished the particulars of the change in the information in time` MEANS
    IF `the notice gives the particulars of the change` AND `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day of the change in the information` `the day the company furnished the notice` 14 Days
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) within 14 days after any change in the information required to be contained in the register ..., particulars of the change" (a period the text fixes in its own words: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a))

-- (d): "within 14 days after the company becomes aware that a person has ceased to be qualified to act as a director of the company by virtue of section 148(1), 154(1), 155(1), 155A(1), 155C(1) or 155D(1), or by a
-- disqualification order made by the Court under section 149, 149A or 154(2) ..., the following information: (i) the fact ...; (ii) the provision ... under which the person ceased to be qualified or the disqualification
-- order was made; (iii) the date on which the person ceased to be qualified".
