-- src:14970 | act as a director of the company;
-- src:14972 | (ii) the provision of this Act under which the person
-- src:14973 | ceased to be qualified to act as a director of the
-- src:14974 | company or the disqualification order was made;
-- src:14976 | (iii) the date on which the person ceased to be qualified to
-- src:14977 | act as a director of the company.
@ref s 173A(1)(d) (src:14959-14977)
GIVEN `the day the company became aware that the person has ceased to be qualified to act as a director of the company by virtue of a provision or order the paragraph names` IS A DATE
      `the day the company furnished the notice` IS A DATE
      `the notice gives the fact that the person has ceased to be qualified to act as a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice gives the provision of this Act under which the person ceased to be qualified or the disqualification order was made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice gives the date on which the person ceased to be qualified to act as a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 173A(1)(d) the company furnished the information about the person's ceasing to be qualified in time` MEANS
    IF    `the notice gives the fact that the person has ceased to be qualified to act as a director of the company`
      AND `the notice gives the provision of this Act under which the person ceased to be qualified or the disqualification order was made`
      AND `the notice gives the date on which the person ceased to be qualified to act as a director of the company`
      AND `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day the company became aware that the person has ceased to be qualified to act as a director of the company by virtue of a provision or order the paragraph names` `the day the company furnished the notice` 14 Days
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(d) within 14 days after the company becomes aware that a person has ceased to be qualified to act as a director ..., the following information" (a period the text fixes in its own words: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a))

-- The four duties as regulative rules. Each is "within 14 days": the day the 14 days run from is the day of the event in the paragraph.
