    ELSE (IF `the notice is in the form the Registrar has determined` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "or, if not prescribed, in such form as the Registrar may determine" (a bare "must" not done: the provision's own question, fork F-164-1)

§ `Section 173B: the duty of the director, chief executive officer, secretary or auditor to tell the company`

DECLARE `s 173B act` IS ONE OF
    `s 173B(1)(a) give the company the information it needs to comply with section 173A(1)(a)`
    `s 173B(1)(b) give the company the information it needs to comply with section 173A(1)(b) or (c)`
    `s 173B(3) furnish the information to the company on its written request`

-- (1)(a): "any information the company needs to comply with section 173A(1)(a) as soon as practicable but not later than 14 days after his or her initial appointment unless he or she has previously given the information
-- to the company in writing". "As soon as practicable" is an open standard the encoder cannot compute: it is a plain input, and the 14 days are the hard limit (fork F-173B-1).
-- src:14998 | 173B.—(1) A director, a chief executive officer, a secretary or an
-- src:14999 | auditor (as the case may be) must give the company —
-- src:15001 | (a) any information the company needs to comply with
-- src:15002 | section 173A(1)(a) as soon as practicable but not later
-- src:15003 | than 14 days after his or her initial appointment unless he
-- src:15004 | or she has previously given the information to the company
-- src:15005 | in writing; and
@ref s 173B(1)(a) (src:14998-15005)
GIVEN `the person has previously given the information to the company in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the person's initial appointment` IS A DATE
      `the day the person gave the information to the company` IS A DATE
      `the person gave the information as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 173B(1)(a) the person has met the requirement to give the company the information` MEANS
    IF `the person has previously given the information to the company in writing`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- the "unless" is met: the requirement is lifted, so the person has not failed it (an "unless" once met: fork F-168-1 reading)
    ELSE IF `the person gave the information as soon as practicable` AND `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day of the person's initial appointment` `the day the person gave the information to the company` 14 Days
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must give the company (a) any information the company needs ... as soon as practicable but not later than 14 days after his or her initial appointment" (a period the text fixes in its own words: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a))

-- (1)(b): "any information the company needs to comply with section 173A(1)(b) or (c) as soon as practicable but not later than 14 days after any change to the information referred to in section 173(3), (5), (6) and (7)".
-- src:15007 | (b) any information the company needs to comply with
-- src:15008 | section 173A(1)(b) or (c) as soon as practicable but not
-- src:15009 | later than 14 days after any change to the information
-- src:15010 | referred to in section 173(3), (5), (6) and (7).
@ref s 173B(1)(b) (src:15007-15010)
GIVEN `the day of the change to the information` IS A DATE
      `the day the person gave the information to the company` IS A DATE
      `the person gave the information as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 173B(1)(b) the person has met the requirement to give the company the information` MEANS
    IF `the person gave the information as soon as practicable` AND `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day of the change to the information` `the day the person gave the information to the company` 14 Days
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must give the company ... (b) any information the company needs ... as soon as practicable but not later than 14 days after any change to the information" (a period the text fixes in its own words: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a))

-- (2): "Despite subsection (1), a director, a chief executive officer, a secretary or an auditor (as the case may be) must, subject to subsection (3), provide any information referred to in section 173(3), (5), (6) or (7)
-- for the purpose of enabling the company to confirm its record of such information or reinstate its record of the information where the original record of the information has been destroyed or lost."
