-- src:15019 | (5), (6) or (7) for the purpose of enabling the company to confirm its
-- src:15020 | record of such information or reinstate its record of the information
-- src:15021 | where the original record of the information has been destroyed or
-- src:15022 | lost.
@ref s 173B(2) (src:15016-15022)
GIVEN `the purpose is to enable the company to confirm its record of the information or to reinstate its record where the original record has been destroyed or lost` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 173B(2) the person must provide the information referred to in section 173(3), (5), (6) or (7)` MEANS
    IF `the purpose is to enable the company to confirm its record of the information or to reinstate its record where the original record has been destroyed or lost`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "must ... provide any information ... for the purpose of enabling the company to confirm its record ... or reinstate its record ... where the original record ... has been destroyed or lost" limits the duty to that purpose, with no "only"

-- (3): "must furnish the information to the company as soon as practicable but not later than 14 days after receipt of a written request for such information from the company."
