      `the day the person furnished the information to the company` IS A DATE
      `the person furnished the information as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 173B(3) the person has met the requirement to furnish the information on request` MEANS
    IF `the person furnished the information as soon as practicable` AND `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day the person received the company's written request for the information` `the day the person furnished the information to the company` 14 Days
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must furnish the information to the company as soon as practicable but not later than 14 days after receipt of a written request" (a period the text fixes in its own words: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a))

-- The duties as regulative rules. The party is a natural person: a director, chief executive officer, secretary or auditor "as the case may be" (the Party type has no constructor for a chief executive officer; Individual is a natural person).
