§ `Section 173C: the consents the company keeps`

DECLARE `s 173C kind of item` IS ONE OF
    `s 173C(a)(i) a signed copy of the director's consent to act as director`
    `s 173C(a)(ii) a statement that the director is not disqualified to act as director under this Act or under any other written law`
    `s 173C(a)(iii) documentary evidence (if any) of any change in the director's name`
    `s 173C(b) a signed copy of the secretary's consent to act as secretary`
    `s 173C some other item`

DECLARE `s 173C act` IS ONE OF
    `s 173C keep at its registered office the signed copy of each director's consent, the statement of non-disqualification, any documentary evidence of a change in name, and the signed copy of each secretary's consent`

-- src:15037 | 173C. Every company must keep at its registered office —
-- src:15038 | (a) in respect of each director —
-- src:15039 | (i) a signed copy of his or her consent to act as director;
-- src:15044 | (ii) a statement that he or she is not disqualified to act as
-- src:15045 | director under this Act or under any other written
-- src:15046 | law; and
-- src:15048 | (iii) documentary evidence (if any) of any change in his
-- src:15049 | or her name; and
-- src:15051 | (b) in respect of a secretary, a signed copy of his or her consent
-- src:15052 | to act as secretary.
@ref s 173C (src:15037-15052)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 173C kind of item`
      `the company keeps the item at its registered office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is documentary evidence of a change in the director's name` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 173C the company has kept the item at its registered office` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 173C some other item` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "Every company must keep at its registered office" lists four items without "only"
    WHEN `s 173C(a)(iii) documentary evidence (if any) of any change in the director's name`
         THEN (IF (NOT `there is documentary evidence of a change in the director's name`) THEN JUST TRUE   -- the paragraph asks for the evidence "(if any)": with none, there is nothing to keep
               ELSE (IF `the company keeps the item at its registered office` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE))   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every company must keep at its registered office (a) in respect of each director ... (iii) documentary evidence (if any) of any change in his or her name" (a bare "must" not done: the provision's own question, fork F-164-1)
    OTHERWISE
         (IF `the company keeps the item at its registered office` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every company must keep at its registered office" the signed copy of consent, the statement and (for a secretary) the signed copy of consent (a bare "must" not done: the provision's own question, fork F-164-1)

-- The duty has no period: "must keep" is a continuing duty with no time, so no breach path ("Rules with no breach path" in NOTES.md).
-- src:15037 | 173C. Every company must keep at its registered office —
-- src:15038 | (a) in respect of each director —
-- src:15039 | (i) a signed copy of his or her consent to act as director;
-- src:15044 | (ii) a statement that he or she is not disqualified to act as
-- src:15045 | director under this Act or under any other written
-- src:15046 | law; and
-- src:15048 | (iii) documentary evidence (if any) of any change in his
-- src:15049 | or her name; and
-- src:15051 | (b) in respect of a secretary, a signed copy of his or her consent
-- src:15052 | to act as secretary.
@ref s 173C (src:15037-15052)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 173C act`
`s 173C the company must keep at its registered office the consents, statements and evidence` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 173C keep at its registered office the signed copy of each director's consent, the statement of non-disqualification, any documentary evidence of a change in name, and the signed copy of each secretary's consent`
    HENCE FULFILLED

§ `Section 173H: penalties`

DECLARE `s 173H penalty` HAS
    `s 173H the highest fine, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `s 173H the person is also liable to a default penalty` IS A BOOLEAN

-- (1): "If default is made by a company in section 173A(1) or 173C, the company and every officer of the company who is in default shall each be guilty of an offence and shall each be liable on conviction to a fine
-- not exceeding $5,000 and also to a default penalty." "Default penalty" is s 4(1)'s term; its amount is not stated here.
-- src:15347 | 173H.—(1) If default is made by a company in section 173A(1) or
-- src:15348 | 173C, the company and every officer of the company who is in
-- src:15349 | default shall each be guilty of an offence and shall each be liable on
-- src:15350 | conviction to a fine not exceeding $5,000 and also to a default
-- src:15351 | penalty.
@ref s 173H(1) (src:15347-15351)
GIVEN `default is made by the company in section 173A(1) or 173C` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 173H(1) the person is guilty of the offence` MEANS
    IF (NOT `default is made by the company in section 173A(1) or 173C`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made by a company in section 173A(1) or 173C, the company and every officer of the company who is in default shall each be guilty of an offence" (a failed "if": marginal reading (a); split site (i), fork F-173H-1 in NOTES.md)
    ELSE IF `the person is the company` OR `the person is an officer of the company who is in default`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the company and every officer of the company who is in default" names who is guilty, with no "only" (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c); split site (i))

-- src:15347 | 173H.—(1) If default is made by a company in section 173A(1) or
-- src:15348 | 173C, the company and every officer of the company who is in
-- src:15349 | default shall each be guilty of an offence and shall each be liable on
-- src:15350 | conviction to a fine not exceeding $5,000 and also to a default
-- src:15351 | penalty.
@ref s 173H(1) (src:15347-15351)
GIVEN `default is made by the company in section 173A(1) or 173C` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 173H penalty`
`s 173H(1) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `default is made by the company in section 173A(1) or 173C` AND (`the person is the company` OR `the person is an officer of the company who is in default`)
    THEN JUST (`s 173H penalty` OF 5000, TRUE)   -- "a fine not exceeding $5,000 and also to a default penalty"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the penalty is that of "the company and every officer of the company who is in default" where "default is made by a company in section 173A(1) or 173C"

-- (2): "A director, a chief executive officer, a secretary or an auditor who fails to comply with any requirement under section 173B shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- $5,000 and also to a default penalty."
-- src:15355 | (2) A director, a chief executive officer, a secretary or an auditor
-- src:15356 | who fails to comply with any requirement under section 173B shall be
-- src:15357 | guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:15358 | exceeding $5,000 and also to a default penalty.
@ref s 173H(2) (src:15355-15358)
GIVEN `the person is a director, chief executive officer, secretary or auditor who fails to comply with a requirement under section 173B` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 173H(2) the person is guilty of the offence` MEANS
    IF `the person is a director, chief executive officer, secretary or auditor who fails to comply with a requirement under section 173B`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A director, a chief executive officer, a secretary or an auditor who fails to comply with any requirement under section 173B shall be guilty" names who is guilty, with no "only" (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c); split site (i), fork F-173H-2 in NOTES.md)

-- src:15355 | (2) A director, a chief executive officer, a secretary or an auditor
-- src:15356 | who fails to comply with any requirement under section 173B shall be
-- src:15357 | guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:15358 | exceeding $5,000 and also to a default penalty.
@ref s 173H(2) (src:15355-15358)
GIVEN `the person is a director, chief executive officer, secretary or auditor who fails to comply with a requirement under section 173B` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 173H penalty`
`s 173H(2) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `the person is a director, chief executive officer, secretary or auditor who fails to comply with a requirement under section 173B`
    THEN JUST (`s 173H penalty` OF 5000, TRUE)   -- "a fine not exceeding $5,000 and also to a default penalty"
